# L1 / B006 — shared script library, settings, add-dependency, angular, api-versioning, architecture-decision.

C R170 OL ARC-020,GOV-017 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL (Reserved) | Reserved decisions need explicit approval: changing an accepted project/architecture decision; adopting a new architectural style or pattern (Rich Domain Model or DDD tactical patterns, CQRS, mediator-based organization, Vertical Slice Architecture, event sourcing, a project-wide Result model, microservices); adding a production project/layer; changing persistence boundaries (e.g. several persistence contexts) or persistence technology; adding an infrastructure category (messaging, background processing, distributed cache, search, external storage, external identity); adding a major library/framework or replacing approved baseline technology; introducing a project-wide convention or abstraction; changing authentication/authorization architecture; a breaking public API change. | engineering decisions | none stated
C R171 OL DEP-017 | DEFAULT | Add the Asp.Versioning Controller integration (Asp.Versioning.Mvc, Asp.Versioning.Mvc.ApiExplorer) only once Controller API versioning has actually been adopted. | API versioning packages | none stated
C R172 OL DEP-004 | MUST | Before installing check whether the exact package/version is deprecated, check known vulnerability information (dotnet package list --vulnerable --include-transitive, the frontend audit command) and verify the exact selected version's license from official registry metadata (and upstream when necessary); permissive licenses (MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD) are acceptable without approval; being free to download does not make a package acceptable. | dependency additions and updates | none stated
C R173 OL DEP-005 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL | Do not install automatically when a package requires payment or a commercial license, or its license has material obligations or cannot be confidently classified (strong copyleft, dual licensing, source-available/custom terms, unclear or missing); present the concern and reasonable alternatives (say so explicitly when none exists), never substitute silently, and make no legal conclusions beyond published license information. | dependency additions | User approval.
C R174 OL GOV-014 | MUST | Keep changes focused on the requested scope and preserve existing behavior unless the task or approved specification requires a change; e.g. after a scanner finding do not automatically replace or upgrade unrelated packages, and do not perform unrelated dependency cleanup during a narrow task. | all changes | Task or approved specification requires change.
C R175 OL GOV-012 | DEFAULT | Prefer simple, maintainable solutions; keep architectural complexity proportional to current requirements; avoid speculative abstractions (e.g. do not wrap every UI-library component in a custom abstraction without a reason). | all code | none stated
C R176 OL WF-016 | DEFAULT | When generated output is wrong or its source contract changes, fix or update the authoritative source (contract, generator configuration) and regenerate; keep generated code separate from handwritten code and do not hand-edit disposable generated output unless the repository intentionally treats it as maintained source. | generated code (e.g. API clients) | Generated output intentionally maintained as source.
C R177 OL API-022 | MUST | When deprecating an externally consumed API version, mark the deprecation in versioning metadata, document the replacement, communicate a realistic migration/removal timeline and keep the old version working for the promised support period; never silently remove a deprecated version. | published API versions | none stated
C R178 OL GOV-017 | MUST | For a Reserved decision send a Decision Request (Context, Options, Recommendation, Blocked, Proceeding with) and continue only with non-Reserved work; do not ask approval for routine choices already constrained by the specification, approved stack, existing code or rules. | Reserved decisions | none stated
C R179 OL GOV-017 | MUST | In autonomous or headless runs take only a policy-compliant non-Reserved path and list unresolved Decision Requests in the final report instead of deciding. | headless/autonomous runs | none stated
C R180 OL GOV-007,GOV-008 | MUST | When a new behavioral rule or tunable value is approved, update the durable source of truth: product behavior in SPECIFICATION.md, tunable values in CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md (then custom-settings). | approved product decisions | none stated
C X16 EX DEP-001,GOV-014 | MUST | Remove dependencies that are no longer used when that is part of the current change and safe to verify; do not leave dead references. | dependency changes | Unrelated dependency cleanup during a narrow task is excluded. | DEP-001 restricts adding dependencies and GOV-014 limits scope; no oracle policy requires removing dependencies made unused by a change. | A refactor that stops using a package must also remove its PackageReference/package.json entry.
C X17 EX WF-009 | MUST | The add-dependency workflow reports package, version, license, vulnerability/deprecation result, target project and approvals obtained or still pending. | dependency changes | none stated | WF-009 covers verification reporting; no oracle policy prescribes dependency-specific report contents. | A dependency addition reported without its license and vulnerability result does not satisfy the workflow.
C X18 EX API-013,ARC-020 | REQUIRES_APPROVAL (Reserved) | Adopting API versioning is Reserved and needs explicit approval, even when a concrete compatibility need exists. | HTTP API versioning | none stated | API-013 allows introducing versioning when a real compatibility need exists and does not require approval; the oracle's consequential-change list does not name API versioning adoption. | With published clients needing coexistence, the agent must still send a Decision Request before adding versioning.
C X19 EX GOV-017,GOV-007 | MUST | Every approved Reserved decision is recorded as an ADR at docs/decisions/NNNN-<kebab-title>.md (Status Accepted with date, Approved by, Context, Decision, Consequences, Alternatives considered; docs/decisions/ created with the first ADR) and summarized as a decision line pointing to the ADR in the decision file of the owning level (frame style rule, decisions.md, frontend stack rule), never in a single cross-level register and without restating rules that live elsewhere. | approved Reserved decisions | Product behavior and tunable values go to SPECIFICATION.md / CUSTOM_SETTINGS.md instead. | GOV-017 requires approval for Reserved changes but no recording artifact; GOV-007 covers product behavior sources only. No oracle policy requires ADR documents or level-stratified decision summaries. | After the user approves adopting Mapster for a new area, the agent must also write an ADR and a decision summary line.
C X20 EX WF-009 | MUST | The architecture-decision workflow reports the decision, ADR path, decision files updated and follow-up work (structure, dependencies, migrations). | decision recording | none stated | No oracle policy prescribes decision-recording report contents. | A recorded decision reported without its ADR path is incomplete.

